course: dictionary
lesson: 2633
title: Feeling without hope
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Despondent means very sad and without hope. A despondent person feels that things will not get better, so they have almost given up.
explain: Look at the words around it. «He's always rather low and despondent when he's wanting his victuals.» Low is another sign of sadness, and the rat is sad because he is missing the food he wants. Victuals is an old word for food.
explain: Despondent is close to dejected and hopeless. Use the swap check: put "very sad and without hope" into the sentence in place of despondent. If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Despondent means very sad and without hope.
fact: Despondent is an adjective, and it can change: despondent, more despondent, most despondent.
fact: Despondent is close in meaning to dejected and hopeless.
fact: Despondent describes a deep, quiet sadness, not a loud or angry one.
exercise: What does despondent mean? | Very hungry | *Very sad and without hope | Very excited and full of energy | Very loud and noisy
exercise: Which word in «He's always rather low and despondent when he's wanting his victuals» shows the mood is sad? | *low | always | wanting | victuals
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to despondent? | delighted | curious | *dejected | noisy
test: Mia reads «despondent» and guesses it means happy. What does it really mean? | Full of joy and hope | Angry and loud | *Very sad and without hope | Calm and sleepy
test: Which sentence shows a character feeling despondent? | They raced to the park and shouted with joy | She laughed and danced all the way home | *He sat by the window, sure that nothing would ever change | The sun was warm and the sea was blue
exam: Which is the correct comparison of despondent? | *more despondent | despondentest | despondently more | despondenter
